==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|swalwe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|swalwa}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*swalwǭ}}. Cognate with {{cog|dum|swaluwe}} (modern {{cog|nl|zwaluw}}), {{cog|osx|swala}}, {{cog|ang|swealwe}} (modern {{cog|en|swallow}}), Old Norse {{m|non|svala}} ({{cog|da|svale}}, {{cog|sv|svala}}).

The football sense from a saying ''„Der fliegt wie ’ne Schwalbe!“'' (“The man flies like a swallow!”), or the like, punning on {{m|de|fliegen}} in the sense of “to fall”. Compare {{m|de|hinfliegen||to fall down}}.

